Description: Show distro pages that should come first, before the built-in pages
 Distro pages in extra-pages/ are appended after the built-in pages, right
 before the last one, so a distro cannot put a page in front of the user first:
 its own introduction, or what a newcomer must know before anything else.
 Pages in first-pages/ (DISTRO_CUSTOM_FIRST_PAGE_FOLDER,
 /usr/share/plasma/plasma-welcome/first-pages/) are shown before the built-in
 Welcome page, after the live installer page in a live environment, sorted by
 name like extra-pages/; --pages finds them too. Nothing changes when the
 folder is absent or empty.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/Sparky-OS/plasma-welcome/tree/order63
Bug-KDE: https://bugs.kde.org/499555
Bug-Upstream: none for this change; searched on 2026-11-25: invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-welcome commits from v6.7.4 to master and Plasma/6.7, its merge requests (distro, custom page, extra, intro, first page, order) and bugs.kde.org product plasma-welcome; bug 499555 asks for more control over the pages and upstream plans it (Oliver Beard, comment 1), with no code yet
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
